---
/* AskBubble.astro — Moss (named Pixel in the code: .pixel-*, the pixel*
   exports and tokens), the tiny design critter who looks after Anupama's
   portfolio and answers the questions a visitor short on time came with.
   Art: Anupama's own watercolour and her 8s clip of him looking around,
   public/images/moss/ — every frame cut out of its backdrop:
   moss-sprite.webp (48 frames, 8x6 grid of 188x223 cells, 4px clear gutter
   so scaled cells can't bleed; same frames-of-the-clip as hero-sprite),
   moss-idle.webp (frame 0), moss-sm.webp (frame 0, panel avatar),
   moss-head.webp (frame 0, header crop). Export recipe: see
   scripts/moss-sprite.py.

   UX reason: a recruiter skimming for 60–90s can get the level, the scope
   and the role she wants in two clicks, and is sent straight to the case
   study or contact that proves it. Every path ends in a link.

   Interaction model follows ozgur.design's "Dobby" chat, studied screen by
   screen, with an original character, her own content and her palette:

   LAUNCHER — Moss himself, sitting on the books in HeroIllustration's
     sprite (feet on the top book: x 565 / y 462 of the 700x980 frame; the
     table and books don't move across the scrub frames, so he stays put
     while the portrait tracks the pointer), with a chat-preview card to
     his right: "Moss" (small, dim, an accent dot) over "Psst…", a tail
     pointing back at him. Moss and the card are one button. At rest the
     only motion is the ellipsis after "Psst" slowly fading in and out
     (static under reduced motion); the words are the "click me" signal. Moss has no
     idle motion; he only answers the pointer, in lockstep with the
     portrait: HeroIllustration dispatches `hero-scrub:frame` whenever it
     draws a new frame and Moss shows the same frame of his own clip
     (looking left, round, up, back),
     so the two share one timeline and can't drift. Over Moss himself he
     also perks up — grows a little from the feet. Fine pointers only (the
     sprite isn't even fetched otherwise); frame 0 and no motion under
     reduced motion, like the portrait. Hover/focus lifts the card and
     opens the offer under "Psst…", "Want the short version?", growing
     right and down (away from her face, never over him); on narrower
     two-column screens the card sits under him instead (.is-below).
     Touch devices show the offer always. The button's
     aria-label carries the full line. Hidden while the panel is open.
     Must sit inside a position:relative box the portrait's size
     (index.astro, .hero__stage).

   PANEL — opens on click (not hover: it's a dialog with a scrim), fixed
     bottom-right, full-width bottom sheet under 640px. Moved to <body> on
     load so no transformed ancestor can trap its position:fixed. Dark and
     monospace throughout on purpose — Pixel's own register, unlike the rest
     of the site — with soft rounded corners (the site's own cards stay
     square). Sequence:
       1. Moss dimmed, "Moss is looking up from the sketchbook…"
       2. he brightens, gives a small hop and a wobble, then types his
          hello; six starter chips
       3. a chip → earlier chips dim and lock, the question appears as the
          visitor's bubble, the header Moss sways while a rotating status
          line shimmers ("Moss is measuring the spacing…"), then the reply types
          out behind an orange caret, followed by link cards, exit buttons
          (email / LinkedIn) and follow-up chips
       4. "That's all, thanks Moss", ×, Escape or the scrim close it; the
          next open starts fresh. ↺ restarts in place.
   Content is the tree in src/data/ask.ts — no model, no backend.

   A11y: role=dialog + aria-modal, focus moves in on open, Tab is kept
   inside, Escape closes and returns focus to the launcher. The typewriter
   is visual only — screen readers get each whole reply once through a
   polite live region. Reduced motion: no shimmer, blink, sway or typing;
   replies appear whole.

   Styles are global but namespaced (.pixel-*) because most of the thread
   is built by the script at runtime and the panel is re-parented to
   <body>, so Astro's scope hash wouldn't reach it. */
import { pixelTree, pixelStatus } from '../data/ask';
const data = JSON.stringify({ tree: pixelTree, status: pixelStatus });

// Moss, as images. States are classes on .pixel-cat: is-asleep (dimmed,
// before he "notices" you), is-happy (a hop), is-waving (a wobble),
// is-thinking (a sway) — see the Moss rules at the end of the styles.
const headCat = `<span class="pixel-cat is-asleep"><img src="/images/moss/moss-head.webp" width="128" height="128" alt="" decoding="async"></span>`;
const bodyCat = `<span class="pixel-cat is-asleep"><img src="/images/moss/moss-sm.webp" width="240" height="287" alt="" decoding="async"></span>`;
---
<div class="pixel-launch">
  <button class="pixel-launcher" type="button" aria-label="Psst… Want the short version? Ask Moss about Anupama’s work" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pixel-panel" aria-haspopup="dialog">
    <span class="pixel-launcher__moss"></span>
    <span class="pixel-launcher__card" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="pixel-launcher__who">Moss</span>
      <span class="pixel-launcher__first">Psst<span class="pixel-launcher__dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
      <span class="pixel-launcher__text"><span>Want the short version?</span></span>
    </span>
  </button>
</div>

<div class="pixel-scrim" data-pixel-scrim></div>
<div class="pixel pixel-panel" id="pixel-panel" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="pixel-title" data-pixel data-tree={data}>
  <div class="pixel-head">
    <p class="pixel-title" id="pixel-title">
      <span class="pixel-head-cat"><Fragment set:html={headCat} /></span>
      <span class="pixel-name">Moss</span> <small>looks after this portfolio</small>
    </p>
    <div class="pixel-actions">
      <button class="pixel-icon-btn" type="button" data-pixel-reset aria-label="Start over">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 3-6.7L3 8"/><path d="M3 3v5h5"/></svg>
      </button>
      <button class="pixel-icon-btn" type="button" data-pixel-close aria-label="Close">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"/></svg>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="pixel-thread" data-pixel-thread></div>
  <div class="u-sr-only" aria-live="polite" data-pixel-live></div>
  <template data-pixel-cat><Fragment set:html={bodyCat} /></template>
</div>

<style is:global>
  /* ================= launcher ================= */
  .pixel-launch {
    /* Moss's feet on the top book: x 565, y 462 in HeroIllustration's
       700x980 frame — left 565/700, bottom (980-462)/980. His cell is the
       clip's full width (the ears reach both edges when he turns), so the
       box is wider than he looks; the translate puts his feet, not the
       box's centre, on that point — feet sit at 53.3% across and 4.6% up
       from the cell's bottom. Floored so he stays findable on the small
       mobile portrait. */
    position: absolute; left: 80.7%; bottom: 52.6%;
    width: max(21%, 3.25rem);
    transform: translate(-53.3%, 4.6%);
    text-align: left;     /* the stacked hero centres its text */
    line-height: normal;
  }
  .pixel-launcher {
    position: relative; display: block; width: 100%; padding: 0; border: 0; background: none; cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--ask-ink); font: 500 0.8125rem/1 var(--font-display);
    transition: opacity var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel), transform var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel);
  }
  /* frame 0 until the sprite has decoded; then the frame the portrait is on */
  .pixel-launcher__moss {
    display: block; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 188 / 223; transform-origin: 53.3% 95.4%;
    background: url('/images/moss/moss-idle.webp') 0 0 / 100% 100% no-repeat;
  }
  .pixel-launcher__moss.has-sprite {
    background-image: url('/images/moss/moss-sprite.webp');
    background-size: 800% 600%;
    background-position: calc(var(--moss-col, 0) * 100% / 7) calc(var(--moss-row, 0) * 100% / 5);
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) and (hover: hover) {
    .pixel-launcher__moss { transition: scale var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel); }
    .pixel-launcher:hover .pixel-launcher__moss, .pixel-launcher:focus-visible .pixel-launcher__moss { scale: 1.08; }
  }
  .pixel-launcher:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--fg); outline-offset: 4px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .pixel-launcher[aria-expanded='true'] { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px); pointer-events: none; }

  /* the card: a chat preview, the first message of a conversation —
     his name, small and dim, over what he's saying, "Psst…" It sits to
     his RIGHT at face level with a tail pointing back at him, so it never
     covers him and grows away from her face. Anchored on its top-left
     corner (percentages of his box, so it tracks him at every portrait
     size). Words at rest are what make it findable — the UX test where a
     visitor nearly missed the old wordless bubble; the only motion at
     rest is the breathing ellipsis. Hover/focus lifts it, darkens the edge and opens the offer,
     "Want the short version?", in the accent under the first line.
     Ground, ink and edge are the page's role colours, so it re-inks in
     dark mode; the accent dot by his name is the only fixed colour. */
  .pixel-launcher__card {
    position: absolute; left: 92%; top: 18%;
    display: grid; justify-items: start; gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.65rem 0.55rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: var(--ask-card-radius);
    background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); box-shadow: var(--ask-card-shadow);
    width: max-content; white-space: nowrap;   /* an absolute box in a ~48px parent would otherwise shrink the words to nothing */
    font-size: var(--ask-launch-step-1); line-height: 1.2;
    transition: border-color var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel), transform var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel);
  }
  /* the tail: a square turned 45deg, two edges drawn, pointing at him */
  .pixel-launcher__card::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; left: calc(var(--ask-card-tail) / -2 - 1px); top: 0.9rem;
    width: var(--ask-card-tail); height: var(--ask-card-tail); background: inherit;
    border-style: solid; border-width: 0 0 1px 1px; border-color: inherit;
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }
  .pixel-launcher:hover .pixel-launcher__card, .pixel-launcher:focus-visible .pixel-launcher__card { border-color: var(--fg-dim); transform: translateY(-1px); }
  .pixel-launcher__who { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; font-size: var(--ask-launch-step-2); color: var(--fg-dim); }
  .pixel-launcher__who::before { content: ''; width: 0.375rem; height: 0.375rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); }
  .pixel-launcher__first { display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; font-size: var(--ask-launch-step-1); }

  /* "Psst…": the ellipsis breathes — all three dots fade slowly between
     full and dim together, Moss has something to say. Chosen over a
     bouncing typing wave as the calmest option. The one motion at rest.
     Static at full strength under reduced motion, a plain "…". */
  .pixel-launcher__dots { display: inline-flex; gap: var(--ask-dot-gap); margin-left: 0.1em; animation: pixel-breathe var(--dur-ask-breathe) ease-in-out infinite; }
  .pixel-launcher__dots i { width: var(--ask-dot); height: var(--ask-dot); border-radius: 50%; background: currentColor; }
  @keyframes pixel-breathe { 0%, 100% { opacity: 1; } 50% { opacity: 0.25; } }

  /* the offer: withheld at rest, opened on hover/focus — 0fr → 1fr on
     both axes so the card grows right and down. --accent-text on --bg
     (5.5:1 light, AA in dark too). Touch has no hover, so there it's
     always shown. */
  .pixel-launcher__text {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0fr; grid-template-rows: 0fr; opacity: 0;
    transition: grid-template-columns 400ms var(--ease-pixel), grid-template-rows 400ms var(--ease-pixel), opacity var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel);
  }
  .pixel-launcher__text > span { overflow: hidden; min-width: 0; min-height: 0; white-space: nowrap; color: var(--accent-text); font-size: var(--ask-launch-step-1); }
  .pixel-launcher:hover .pixel-launcher__text, .pixel-launcher:focus-visible .pixel-launcher__text { grid-template-columns: 1fr; grid-template-rows: 1fr; opacity: 1; }
  @media (hover: none) { .pixel-launcher__text { grid-template-columns: 1fr; grid-template-rows: 1fr; opacity: 1; } }

  /* BELOW HIM, when the right side is short: on narrower two-column
     screens (roughly 860–1280px) the portrait sits close to the content
     edge and the open card would run off it. There the card drops under
     the books, onto the table, anchored top-right so it opens down and
     to the left, with the tail on its top edge pointing up at him.
     (Above his head was tried — it covered her face.) Decided on load
     and resize (the script sets .is-below), never on hover, so the card
     doesn't jump under the pointer. */
  .pixel-launch.is-below .pixel-launcher__card { left: auto; right: 4%; top: 108%; justify-items: end; }
  .pixel-launch.is-below .pixel-launcher__card::before { left: auto; right: 1rem; top: calc(var(--ask-card-tail) / -2 - 1px); transform: rotate(135deg); }

  /* ================= panel ================= */
  .pixel-scrim {
    position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 1000; background: var(--pixel-scrim);
    opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; transition: opacity var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel);
  }
  .pixel-scrim.is-open { opacity: 1; pointer-events: auto; }

  .pixel-panel {
    position: fixed; right: 1.25rem; bottom: 1.25rem; z-index: 1001;
    width: min(26rem, calc(100vw - 2.5rem)); height: min(40rem, calc(100svh - 2.5rem));
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--pixel-bg); color: var(--pixel-fg);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pixel-panel); box-shadow: var(--pixel-shadow);
    font-family: var(--font-mono); text-align: left;
    opacity: 0; transform: translateY(12px); visibility: hidden; pointer-events: none;
    transition: opacity var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel), transform var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel), visibility 0s var(--dur-pixel);
  }
  .pixel-panel.is-open { opacity: 1; transform: none; visibility: visible; pointer-events: auto; transition-delay: 0s; }

  .pixel-head { flex: none; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; padding: 1.1rem 1.1rem 1.1rem 1.4rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--pixel-rule); }
  .pixel-title { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.625rem; margin: 0; font: 500 var(--pixel-step-title)/1 var(--font-mono); }
  .pixel-name { white-space: nowrap; }   /* two words; the tagline wraps instead */
  .pixel-title small { font: 400 var(--pixel-step-small)/1.3 var(--font-mono); color: var(--pixel-dim); }
  .pixel-head-cat { display: inline-flex; }
  .pixel-head-cat .pixel-cat { width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 50%; overflow: hidden; background: var(--ask-bg); }
  .pixel-actions { display: flex; gap: 0.25rem; }
  .pixel-icon-btn {
    width: 2rem; height: 2rem; display: grid; place-items: center; border: 0; border-radius: 50%;
    background: none; color: var(--pixel-dim); cursor: pointer;
    transition: background var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel), color var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel);
  }
  .pixel-icon-btn:hover { background: var(--pixel-high); color: var(--pixel-fg); }
  .pixel-icon-btn svg { width: 1rem; height: 1rem; }

  .pixel-thread { flex: 1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem 1.5rem; overflow-y: auto; overscroll-behavior: contain; scrollbar-width: none; }
  .pixel-thread::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
  .pixel-avatar { align-self: center; padding: 0.75rem 0; animation: pixel-rise var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel) both; }
  .pixel-avatar .pixel-cat { width: 88px; }

  .pixel-msg { max-width: 92%; font: 400 var(--pixel-step-body)/var(--pixel-leading) var(--font-mono); animation: pixel-rise var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel) both; }
  .pixel-msg p { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .pixel-msg p:last-child { margin: 0; }
  .pixel-msg strong { font-weight: 500; color: var(--pixel-fg); }
  .pixel-msg--user {
    align-self: flex-end; background: var(--pixel-high); font-size: var(--pixel-step-body); line-height: 1.45;
    padding: 0.6rem 1rem; border-radius: var(--radius-pixel-msg) var(--radius-pixel-msg) 6px var(--radius-pixel-msg);
  }
  .pixel-msg--bot { align-self: flex-start; }
  @keyframes pixel-rise { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(6px); } }

  /* status: dots + a shimmering, rotating line */
  .pixel-status { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: var(--pixel-step-small); line-height: 1; color: var(--pixel-dim); white-space: nowrap; }
  .pixel-status__dots { display: inline-flex; gap: 3px; }
  .pixel-status__dots i { width: 4px; height: 4px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--pixel-dim); animation: pixel-blink 1.2s infinite; }
  .pixel-status__dots i:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 0.2s; }
  .pixel-status__dots i:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 0.4s; }
  @keyframes pixel-blink { 0%, 100% { opacity: 0.25; } 50% { opacity: 1; } }
  .pixel-shimmer {
    color: transparent;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--pixel-dim) 0%, var(--pixel-dim) 40%, var(--pixel-fg) 50%, var(--pixel-dim) 60%, var(--pixel-dim) 100%);
    background-size: 220% 100%; -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text;
    animation: pixel-shimmer 1.5s linear infinite;
  }
  @keyframes pixel-shimmer { from { background-position: 100% 0; } to { background-position: -120% 0; } }

  .pixel-cursor::after {
    content: ''; display: inline-block; width: 0.5ch; height: 1em; margin-left: 2px; vertical-align: -0.15em;
    background: var(--pixel-accent); animation: pixel-caret 1.06s steps(2, jump-none) infinite;
  }
  @keyframes pixel-caret { 50% { opacity: 0; } }

  .pixel-card {
    display: block; margin-top: 0.75rem; padding: 0.95rem 1.1rem; text-decoration: none;
    background: var(--pixel-raised); border: 1px solid var(--pixel-rule-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-pixel-card);
    transition: border-color var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel), background var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel);
  }
  .pixel-card:hover { border-color: var(--pixel-accent); background: var(--pixel-high); }
  .pixel-card__label { font-size: var(--step-label); letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label); text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--pixel-dim); margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .pixel-card__title { color: var(--pixel-fg); font-size: var(--pixel-step-body); font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.35; }
  .pixel-card__sub { color: var(--pixel-dim); font-size: var(--pixel-step-small); margin-top: 0.15rem; }

  .pixel-chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: 0.25rem; animation: pixel-rise var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel) both; }
  .pixel-chip {
    display: inline-block; padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem; border: 1px solid var(--pixel-rule-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: none; color: var(--pixel-fg); font: 400 var(--pixel-step-small)/1.3 var(--font-mono); text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer;
    transition: background var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel), border-color var(--dur-pixel) var(--ease-pixel);
  }
  .pixel-chip:hover { border-color: var(--pixel-fg); background: var(--pixel-high); }
  /* exits: filled like the site's primary button */
  .pixel-chip--exit {
    background: var(--pixel-fg); border-color: var(--pixel-fg); color: var(--pixel-bg);
    font-size: var(--pixel-step-small); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label); text-transform: uppercase; padding: 0.65rem 1.15rem;
  }
  .pixel-chip--exit:hover { background: var(--pixel-fg); opacity: 0.86; }
  .pixel-chips.is-done .pixel-chip { opacity: 0.35; pointer-events: none; }

  .pixel-icon-btn:focus-visible, .pixel-chip:focus-visible, .pixel-card:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--pixel-accent); outline-offset: 2px; }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .pixel-panel { left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; width: 100%; height: 88dvh; border-radius: var(--radius-pixel-panel) var(--radius-pixel-panel) 0 0; transform: translateY(24px); }
    .pixel-chip { padding: 0.7rem 1rem; }   /* same size as desktop, taller tap target */
    .pixel-thread { padding-inline: 1.25rem; }
  }

  /* ================= Moss ================= */
  .pixel-cat { display: block; transform-origin: 50% 100%; transition: opacity 0.4s var(--ease-pixel), filter 0.4s var(--ease-pixel); }
  .pixel-cat img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .pixel-cat.is-asleep { opacity: 0.55; filter: saturate(0.4); }
  .pixel-cat.is-happy { animation: pixel-hop 0.5s var(--ease-pixel); }
  @keyframes pixel-hop { 40% { transform: translateY(-6%); } }
  .pixel-cat.is-waving { animation: pixel-wave 0.4s ease-in-out 4 alternate; }
  @keyframes pixel-wave { from { transform: rotate(-3deg); } to { transform: rotate(3deg); } }
  .pixel-cat.is-thinking { animation: pixel-tilt 1.6s ease-in-out infinite; }
  @keyframes pixel-tilt { 0%, 100% { transform: rotate(-6deg); } 50% { transform: rotate(6deg); } }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .pixel-launcher, .pixel-launcher__card, .pixel-launcher__text, .pixel-launcher__dots, .pixel-scrim, .pixel-panel,
    .pixel-panel *, .pixel-cat, .pixel-cat * { animation: none !important; transition: none !important; }
    .pixel-shimmer { color: var(--pixel-dim); background: none; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  interface Card { label: string; title: string; sub: string; href: string }
  interface Exit { label: string; href: string; external?: boolean }
  interface Node { q: string; say: string[]; cards?: Card[]; exits?: Exit[]; next?: string[] }

  const panel = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-pixel]');
  const launcher = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.pixel-launcher');
  const scrim = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-pixel-scrim]');

  // Moss plays the frame the portrait is on (HeroIllustration dispatches
  // `hero-scrub:frame`); both clips are the same 48 frames of an 8s, 24fps
  // timeline. The sprite is only fetched where the portrait scrubs — the
  // same fine-pointer, full-motion test HeroIllustration uses — and is
  // swapped in once decoded, so he never flashes blank.
  const stage = launcher?.closest<HTMLElement>('.hero__stage');
  const moss = launcher?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.pixel-launcher__moss');
  if (stage && moss && !matchMedia('(hover: none), (pointer: coarse)').matches
      && !matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
    const COLS = 8;
    const sprite = new Image();
    sprite.src = '/images/moss/moss-sprite.webp';
    sprite.decode().then(() => moss.classList.add('has-sprite')).catch(() => {});
    stage.addEventListener('hero-scrub:frame', (e) => {
      const { frame } = (e as CustomEvent<{ frame: number }>).detail;
      moss.style.setProperty('--moss-col', String(frame % COLS));
      moss.style.setProperty('--moss-row', String(Math.floor(frame / COLS)));
    });
  }

  // The card opens to Moss's right when the open card stays clear of the
  // screen edge — it may run into the outer two-thirds of --gutter (it's
  // a hover note, not layout), never closer to the edge than that — otherwise under him (.is-below, see the
  // styles). Measured with the words' full width, so it's decided before
  // anyone hovers; re-checked on resize.
  const launch = launcher?.closest<HTMLElement>('.pixel-launch');
  const words = launcher?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.pixel-launcher__text > span');
  if (launch && words) {
    // --gutter is a clamp()/max() expression; a probe element resolves it to px
    const probe = document.createElement('div');
    probe.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;visibility:hidden;height:0;width:var(--gutter)';
    document.body.append(probe);
    const place = () => {
      launch.classList.remove('is-below');
      const label = launch.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.pixel-launcher__card')!;
      const pad = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(label).paddingLeft) * 2;
      const right = label.getBoundingClientRect().left + Math.max(words.scrollWidth, label.offsetWidth - pad) + pad;
      const gutter = probe.getBoundingClientRect().width;
      launch.classList.toggle('is-below', right > document.documentElement.clientWidth - gutter / 3);
    };
    place();
    document.fonts?.ready.then(place);
    let raf = 0;
    addEventListener('resize', () => { cancelAnimationFrame(raf); raf = requestAnimationFrame(place); });
  }

  if (panel && launcher && scrim) {
    // Re-parent so no transformed ancestor (e.g. Reveal) can trap position:fixed.
    document.body.append(scrim, panel);

    const { tree, status } = JSON.parse(panel.dataset.tree!) as { tree: Record<string, Node>; status: string[] };
    const thread = panel.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-pixel-thread]')!;
    const live = panel.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-pixel-live]')!;
    const catTpl = panel.querySelector<HTMLTemplateElement>('[data-pixel-cat]')!;
    const head = panel.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.pixel-head-cat .pixel-cat')!;
    const closeBtn = panel.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-pixel-close]')!;
    const reduce = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    const wait = (ms: number) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, reduce ? 0 : ms));
    let run = 0;          // bumped on close/reset; an in-flight reply checks it and stops
    let started = false;

    const el = <K extends keyof HTMLElementTagNameMap>(tag: K, cls?: string, html?: string) => {
      const e = document.createElement(tag);
      if (cls) e.className = cls;
      if (html != null) e.innerHTML = html;   // only ever our own static strings from ask.ts
      return e;
    };
    const scrollEnd = () => { thread.scrollTop = thread.scrollHeight; };
    const pulse = (c: Element, cls: string, ms: number) => { c.classList.add(cls); setTimeout(() => c.classList.remove(cls), ms); };
    const setAsleep = (c: Element) => c.setAttribute('class', 'pixel-cat is-asleep');
    const statusEl = (text: string) => {
      const s = el('span', 'pixel-status', '<span class="pixel-status__dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="pixel-shimmer"></span>');
      s.querySelector('.pixel-shimmer')!.textContent = text;
      return s;
    };

    async function typeInto(p: HTMLElement, html: string, id: number) {
      const text = el('div', undefined, html).textContent ?? '';
      if (!reduce) {
        p.classList.add('pixel-cursor');
        for (let i = 1; i <= text.length; i++) {
          if (id !== run) return;
          p.textContent = text.slice(0, i);
          if (i % 4 === 0) scrollEnd();
          await wait(text[i - 1] === '.' ? 90 : 14);
        }
        p.classList.remove('pixel-cursor');
      }
      p.innerHTML = html;
    }

    async function say(key: string, id: number) {
      const node = tree[key];
      const msg = el('div', 'pixel-msg pixel-msg--bot');
      thread.append(msg);
      scrollEnd();

      if (key !== 'start') {
        head.classList.add('is-thinking');
        const s = statusEl('');
        msg.append(s);
        for (let k = 0; k < 2 && id === run; k++) {
          s.querySelector('.pixel-shimmer')!.textContent = status[(Math.random() * status.length) | 0];
          await wait(k === 0 ? 900 : 1100);
        }
        s.remove();
        head.classList.remove('is-thinking');
      }
      if (id !== run) return;

      for (const para of node.say) {
        const p = el('p');
        msg.append(p);
        await typeInto(p, para, id);
        if (id !== run) return;
      }
      (node.cards ?? []).forEach((c) => {
        const a = el('a', 'pixel-card', '<div class="pixel-card__label"></div><div class="pixel-card__title"></div><div class="pixel-card__sub"></div>');
        a.href = c.href;
        a.querySelector('.pixel-card__label')!.textContent = c.label;
        a.querySelector('.pixel-card__title')!.textContent = c.title;
        a.querySelector('.pixel-card__sub')!.textContent = c.sub;
        msg.append(a);
      });
      if (key !== 'start') pulse(head, 'is-happy', 700);
      live.textContent = msg.textContent ?? '';   // the whole reply, once

      const chips = el('div', 'pixel-chips');
      (node.exits ?? []).forEach((x) => {
        const a = el('a', 'pixel-chip pixel-chip--exit');
        a.href = x.href;
        a.textContent = x.label;
        if (x.external) {
          a.target = '_blank';
          a.rel = 'noopener';
          const arrow = el('span', undefined, ' ↗');
          arrow.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
          a.append(arrow);
        }
        chips.append(a);
      });
      (node.next ?? []).forEach((k) => {
        const b = el('button', 'pixel-chip');
        b.type = 'button';
        b.textContent = tree[k].q;
        b.addEventListener('click', () => pick(k, chips));
        chips.append(b);
      });
      thread.append(chips);
      scrollEnd();
      // keep keyboard focus in the conversation: land on the first new chip
      chips.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.pixel-chip')?.focus({ preventScroll: true });
    }

    async function pick(key: string, chips: HTMLElement) {
      chips.classList.add('is-done');
      chips.querySelectorAll('button').forEach((b) => { b.disabled = true; });
      if (key === 'bye') { close(); return; }
      closeBtn.focus({ preventScroll: true });   // the chip just got disabled; don't drop focus to <body>
      const q = el('div', 'pixel-msg pixel-msg--user');
      q.textContent = tree[key].q;
      thread.append(q);
      scrollEnd();
      await say(key, run);
    }

    async function start() {
      const id = ++run;
      started = true;
      thread.replaceChildren();
      setAsleep(head);
      const av = el('div', 'pixel-avatar');
      av.append(catTpl.content.cloneNode(true));
      const big = av.querySelector('.pixel-cat')!;
      thread.append(av);
      const wake = el('div', 'pixel-msg pixel-msg--bot');
      wake.append(statusEl('Moss is looking up from the sketchbook…'));
      thread.append(wake);
      await wait(1300);
      if (id !== run) return;
      wake.remove();
      big.classList.remove('is-asleep');
      head.classList.remove('is-asleep');
      pulse(big, 'is-happy', 500);
      setTimeout(() => pulse(big, 'is-waving', 1600), 250);
      await say('start', id);
    }

    const isOpen = () => panel.classList.contains('is-open');
    function open() {
      panel!.classList.add('is-open');
      scrim!.classList.add('is-open');
      launcher!.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
      closeBtn.focus({ preventScroll: true });
      if (!started) start();
    }
    function close() {
      panel!.classList.remove('is-open');
      scrim!.classList.remove('is-open');
      launcher!.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
      run++;
      started = false;   // next open starts fresh, asleep
      setAsleep(head);
      launcher!.focus({ preventScroll: true });
    }

    launcher.addEventListener('click', open);
    scrim.addEventListener('click', close);
    closeBtn.addEventListener('click', close);
    panel.querySelector('[data-pixel-reset]')!.addEventListener('click', () => { start(); });
    document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if (!isOpen()) return;
      if (e.key === 'Escape') { close(); return; }
      if (e.key === 'Tab') {
        const f = [...panel.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('button:not(:disabled), a[href]')];
        if (!f.length) return;
        const first = f[0], last = f[f.length - 1];
        if (e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === first) { e.preventDefault(); last.focus(); }
        else if (!e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === last) { e.preventDefault(); first.focus(); }
      }
    });
  }
</script>
